5. Deployment & Testing Commands

1.Lint and validate chart syntax:

Make sure you are in the parent directory containing the k8s-mini-project-1 folder:

helm lint ./k8s-mini-project-1

Verification: Should output 1 chart(s) linted, 0 chart(s) failed.

2.Dry-run rendering (check generated YAML):

Inspect how templates resolve without modifying cluster state:

helm install mini-app ./k8s-mini-project-1 --dry-run --debug

3.Deploy to a fresh namespace:

Deploy the complete stack in an isolated release:

helm install mini-app ./k8s-mini-project-1 -n mini-project-helm --create-namespace

4.Verify all resources are up:

kubectl get all,pvc,ingress,hpa -n mini-project-helm

Verification: You will see 2 frontend pods, 1 redis-0 pod, 1 bounded PVC, Ingress pointing to myapp.local,
 and the HPA targeting the deployment.
 
5.Perform an in-place configuration update:

Change replica count dynamically using CLI overrides:

helm upgrade mini-app ./k8s-mini-project-1 -n mini-project-helm --set frontend.replicaCount=3

kubectl get pods -n mini-project-helm -l app=frontend

